{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/74913-can-anything-else-be-installed-into-a-gadget","id":74913,"title":"Can anything else be Installed into a Gadget?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-19T05:41:05-08:00","id":74913,"title":"Can anything else be Installed into a Gadget?","content":"Specifically, can an Interlock be Installed? And also is it possible to consider a pact (the physical document) a type of Gadget that has some sort of reality altering effect installed into it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T07:33:35-08:00","id":74952,"title":"","content":"There are apparently going to be rules for installing demonic form powers into Gadgets in the Player's Guide; presumably that's what the length of chain that saps Aether in How An Angel Dies is.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure pacts aren't considered Gadgets by any reasonable stretch of the term, unaccompanied by special effects or active uses as they are.<br /> <br /> Interlocks specifically modifying Installation is a thing I could see happening, but not as a general thing; they're the demon's personal powers and innately being able to give them to anyone doesn't seem like the sort of thing the Unchained as a whole would be likely to go for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T18:19:04-08:00","id":75356,"title":"","content":"bit of a quibble here but a gadget is the end result of having successfully installed an embed and an exploit into an item. So with that in mind. I don't think you can further alter a gadget to add any other embeds or exploits into it (or anything else). That said,I have no rules or page numbers to offer up as evidence. As always, consider your ST/gaming group/the narrative.<br /> <br /> As to whether an interlock can be installed, I'd be inclined to say no. Again, I don't have any specific rules to reference, save the fact that the book is silent on it.<br /> I'm against this because interlocks are, in my view, too personal. Whatever they are, interlocks seem to only result when a specific demon combines two universal processes in a way that no other demon can reproduce. Indeed two demons who somehow have the exact same keys in the exact same order may end up with wildly different Interlocks (EDIT: was going to example time this but I think I'll post them in the interlock thread instead).<br /> <br /> My point is that Interlocks are intensely personal and I don't see very many demons who would be willing to put that much of themselves into another object. Not to say that it can't be done... that's up to your ST/Group/the narrative.<br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to the second question. I think that the pact in and of itself is just paper (or whatever it is that you wrote the contract on). Though for the sake of argument, the pact that could possibly, remotely, be considered more gadget-y than others would be the soul pact as a willpower dot is expended during it's creation. (I know, I know, the reasons, metaphysics and systems in play are completely different so it's definitely, totally overreaching).<br /> <br /> <br /> Though kind of tangent but related to pacts and gadgets. One of the more established, and more powerful demon npcs that I've kept in reserve (for a higher tier game) has a number of his most important soul pacts stored the following way; in a small iron box, in a small silver box, stored in a lead box inscribed with anti-scrying/detection runes (straight up, good-old fashioned occult). The lead box is also a gadget with the cause and effect embed which triggers when the box is opened causing an unlikely (and often fatal) accident to occur. That said, he also has them dropped in the foundations of new high rise developments in various cities <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Definitely not paranoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","user":"Rixx","date":"some clarification. 02-19-2014, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T11:46:02-08:00","id":78473,"title":"","content":"There's a whole chapter on gadgets in the Players Guide, while some new and interesting stuff. We didn't address installing an Interlock into a gadget (balls, we should have), but I'd treat it like a near-field gadget.<br /> <br /> That'll make more sense when the book comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:39:08-08:00","id":80568,"title":"","content":"Pretty much agree with the whole group consensus here, it really should just be up to the group and ST to decide if you come across an issue that hasn't been addressed. As for gadget installation, my group has ruled only one embed per item but we're allowing them to be installed on different components/extensions of the same item and have them all used together.<br /> <br /> Example: We can have Merciless Gunman installed on a hand gun, Hush installed on the silencer, Hellfire installed on the clip, Deafen installed on the hammer and Check Backdrop installed on the scope. Now you have a horrible horrible murder machine...... hmmmm, I want that now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:15:41-08:00","id":80596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheFrigidMidget</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/74913-can-anything-else-be-installed-into-a-gadget?p=80568#post80568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much agree with the whole group consensus here, it really should just be up to the group and ST to decide if you come across an issue that hasn't been addressed. As for gadget installation, my group has ruled only one embed per item but we're allowing them to be installed on different components/extensions of the same item and have them all used together.<br /> <br /> Example: We can have Merciless Gunman installed on a hand gun, Hush installed on the silencer, Hellfire installed on the clip, Deafen installed on the hammer and Check Backdrop installed on the scope. Now you have a horrible horrible murder machine...... hmmmm, I want that now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I like the gun analogy. One concept I keep thinking of is modern cell phones. Once you had a cell phone that was only a cell phone, now it is a phone, camera, computer, pager/text, calender, map..etc. I would really like to stick multiple functions on the apps themselves to take advantage of their multiple uses. For example, put 'tag and release' on maps and you suddenly have the best GPS device to track people. Have 'identity theft' linked to the photo/picture program that you can use on anybody you take a picture of, attach 'hearts desire' to the facebook/social app so you can get what people really want, or perhaps social dynamics so you know what the real relationship to everyone is, or even 'force relationship' to manipulate/change peoples relationships on the program, What about slapping 'sermon' on your video recording app? Anybody who watches the video you post will fall under your sway? Just something that has been in the back of my mind for a while. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T04:22:46-08:00","id":82039,"title":"","content":"To reverse the question, what are the limits for what can act as hardware?<br /> 1. Supernatural objects can't act as hardware but can non-supernatural infrastructure act as hardware?<br /> 2. Are there size restrictions? Can a building act as hardware? A ship?<br /> 3. How contained does hardware have to be? E.g. if I install something into a full bottle of milk and then spill the milk in many different locations? Or if I install something into a batter can the effect of the embed be spread into devices that are charged using that battery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T00:14:13-08:00","id":82537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/74913-can-anything-else-be-installed-into-a-gadget?p=80596#post80596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I like the gun analogy. One concept I keep thinking of is modern cell phones. Once you had a cell phone that was only a cell phone, now it is a phone, camera, computer, pager/text, calender, map..etc. I would really like to stick multiple functions on the apps themselves to take advantage of their multiple uses. For example, put 'tag and release' on maps and you suddenly have the best GPS device to track people. Have 'identity theft' linked to the photo/picture program that you can use on anybody you take a picture of, attach 'hearts desire' to the facebook/social app so you can get what people really want, or perhaps social dynamics so you know what the real relationship to everyone is, or even 'force relationship' to manipulate/change peoples relationships on the program, What about slapping 'sermon' on your video recording app? Anybody who watches the video you post will fall under your sway? Just something that has been in the back of my mind for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like that idea but I don't think our story teller would allow the installation of embeds into software or apps. From what I remember all the samples and descriptions of gadgets seem to need a physical object to support the embed. He may allow the dismantling of the phone to install Identity Theft on the camera, Catch and Release on the GPS receiver, Momentum on the battery and maybe Voice of the Machine on the speaker or something. If you're in a game I'd just speak to your ST and discuss it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/74913-can-anything-else-be-installed-into-a-gadget?p=82039#post82039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To reverse the question, what are the limits for what can act as hardware?<br /> 1. Supernatural objects can't act as hardware but can non-supernatural infrastructure act as hardware?<br /> 2. Are there size restrictions? Can a building act as hardware? A ship?<br /> 3. How contained does hardware have to be? E.g. if I install something into a full bottle of milk and then spill the milk in many different locations? Or if I install something into a batter can the effect of the embed be spread into devices that are charged using that battery?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I thought all infrastructure was supernatural. Or are you just meaning mundane roads, buildings etc? I'd say no anyway, just because the flavour of gadgets is meant to be James Bondish type stuff that the demon can whip out to get herself out of a pinch. But that being said story comes first so if it makes sense in the story or actually serves a purpose then I'd say yes. I'm very easily swayed lol.<br /> <br /> 2. There isn't any mention of size restrictions in the book. In fact the only mention I can find is <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent - page 188</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consideration should be taken for an object\u2019s Size and construction; sturdier devices are more difficult to alter.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the story teller might attach a -2 penalty or whatever to the installation roll. The time taken would be longer and the actual installation roll would need to get a number of successes equal to the objects structure if embedding or double that if exploiting.<br /> <br /> 3. I'd assume you'd be installing the embed on the actual bottle itself seing as the milk is a consumable and would quickly go off and need to be thrown out. Seems like a waste of a perfectly good will power point. Regarding the battery idea, remember that when installing embeds the object has to be synergistic to said embed or share a common function. If you were to install an exploit into the battery then you would warp the physical properties of the battery to the point where you could not fit it back in its slot so you'd have to have a weird alien flashing battery that you'd need to hook it up to devices externally. That would pretty much be pointless though as whatever function the battery provided, you could just use the battery instead of hooking it up to another object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}